Session 5, 2026-09-05, Ag Leader InCommand 1200 (New Holland tractor).
Run 2 -- first capture with the new vtstat=<count>/<age-ms> counter
(IsobusVtInterface::GetVtStatusMessageCount()/GetVtStatusMessageAgeMs()),
natural behaviour, updateVtVariables() NOT yet disabled (see run 3 for the
isolation test that ruled it out as the cause). Firmware: isobus-tc-client
at a5db807 plus the new counter, uncommitted at the time of this run.

Timestamps are seconds since the logging script attached to COM4, which in
this run happened after the board had already fully booted, so t=0 does not
correspond to board reset.

Lines from t=9.8 to t=126.9 repeat the same steady-state
(vt=N(0/22) vtstat=4/<growing age>ms, msgs= climbing ~31/s, aiso= climbing
1/s, busload steady ~17%) with no change of any kind -- trimmed here to the
first and last few for brevity. The full, untrimmed capture is available in
this session's transcript if more granularity is ever needed.

